          "secNumber": "3.5",
          "heading": "Lesson 3.2 \u2014 Boundary shear and sediment entrainment",
          "content": "### Process mechanism and scale\n\nFluid drag and submerged particle weight determine approximate entrainment thresholds, often summarized by dimensionless Shields stress. Draw a control volume showing forcing, material transfers and storage. Name the scale and timescale of the proposed process; landform shape alone does not reveal either.\n\n### Observable evidence\n\nBed-surface grain size, riffle mobility, water-surface slope and transport samples constrain motion. Record surveyed discharge section, particle size and stage observations. In the diagram of a downstream profile, two bar maps and time-integrated transport samples, label measured features separately from inferred histories. Provide survey dates, scale and a detection threshold.\n\n### Alternatives and field tests\n\nA bed may remain immobile at high apparent stress if armoring or cohesion resists motion. Compute Shields stress for two grain sizes under an assumed hydraulic radius and slope; compare measured bed fractions. Consider changing roughness mistaken for a change in sediment supply. Identify one independently measurable outcome that would distinguish the two interpretations, and one negative result that would undermine the leading explanation.\n\n### Worked quantitative example \u2014 Shields stress screening\n\n**Given.** Water density 1000, grain density 2650 kg/m\u00b3, hydraulic radius 1.5 m, slope .006, grain diameter .020 m. **Calculation:** 1000\u00d71.5\u00d70.006 / [(2650\u22121000)\u00d70.020]. **Result:** **0.27273 dimensionless**. Work through the units before using the output to discuss Earth-surface history. Doubling the grain size halves the dimensionless stress in this simple fixed-flow comparison. Grain packing and cohesion alter real incipient-motion thresholds. A correct result from an incorrect conceptual model is not evidence that the process operated. State which measured variable would need independent verification. If the answer is a rate, indicate the averaging interval; if it is a geometric ratio, identify the scale and measurement direction; if it is a budget, give the boundary and the sign convention.\n\n### Research procedure and critical interpretation\n\nDocument hydrograph timing; independently check cross-sectional integration. Assess sensitivity to supply/transport separation and verify stage comparability. Record each raw observation, units, uncertainty and assumptions before model fitting.\n\nThreshold values vary with grain Reynolds number, packing and mixture, so one constant is not universal. Call the outcome a screening calculation, not proof that grains moved. A high-resolution shape map without ages and a dated deposit without spatial coverage offer different constraints. Explain how they could be combined for boundary shear and sediment entrainment without overclaiming a process history. Identify one further test.\n\n### Problems with answer guidance\n\n**Problem 1.** Recalculate the worked case after changing an input by 20% and show units. **Problem 2.** Contrast two possible landform origins using a specific field test. **Answer guidance:** correct units, explicit physical assumptions and a genuinely distinguishing observation are essential.",
