          "heading": "Lesson 6.4 \u2014 Delta growth, avulsion and sediment trapping",
          "content": "### Process mechanism and scale\n\nDeltas build where river sediment enters a receiving basin, but waves, tides, subsidence and upstream dams alter storage and lobe development. Draw a control volume showing forcing, material transfers and storage. Name the scale and timescale of the proposed process; landform shape alone does not reveal either.\n\n### Observable evidence\n\nDistributary patterns, mouth bars, dated delta-front strata and satellite imagery constrain sediment routing. Record wave direction, tidal datum, survey dates and sediment sources. In the diagram of repeat profile, mapped shoreline and bounded littoral sediment budget, label measured features separately from inferred histories. Provide survey dates, scale and a detection threshold.\n\n### Alternatives and field tests\n\nA retreating delta edge may occur despite local channel deposition if offshore losses exceed supply. Measure hypothetical sediment delivery above and below a reservoir and compute a coarse storage balance. Consider beach seasonal exchange mistaken for permanent coastal erosion. Identify one independently measurable outcome that would distinguish the two interpretations, and one negative result that would undermine the leading explanation.\n\n### Worked quantitative example \u2014 Reservoir sediment retention\n\n**Given.** 420,000 tonnes/yr incoming sediment and an illustrative retention fraction of .70. **Calculation:** 420000 \u00d7 0.70. **Result:** **294,000 tonnes/yr**. Work through the units before using the output to discuss Earth-surface history. Different grain sizes can have different retention efficiencies. Dry-mass trapping is not directly an estimate of coastal delta volume. A correct result from an incorrect conceptual model is not evidence that the process operated. State which measured variable would need independent verification. If the answer is a rate, indicate the averaging interval; if it is a geometric ratio, identify the scale and measurement direction; if it is a budget, give the boundary and the sign convention.\n\n### Research procedure and critical interpretation\n\nDocument datum consistency; independently check sediment cell boundaries. Assess sensitivity to tidal timing and verify land-level motion. Record each raw observation, units, uncertainty and assumptions before model fitting.\n\nSurface area alone cannot quantify sediment volume or sediment quality. Connect shoreline changes to fluxes through an explicitly drawn control volume. A high-resolution shape map without ages and a dated deposit without spatial coverage offer different constraints. Explain how they could be combined for delta growth, avulsion and sediment trapping without overclaiming a process history. Identify one further test.\n\n### Problems with answer guidance\n\n**Problem 1.** Recalculate the worked case after changing an input by 20% and show units. **Problem 2.** Contrast two possible landform origins using a specific field test. **Answer guidance:** correct units, explicit physical assumptions and a genuinely distinguishing observation are essential.",
